# ── Accepted / Ignored Vulnerabilities ──
# Each CVE is documented with the technical reason it is not exploitable
# in the Fyona ERP production environment.
# Review this file whenever python-jose or starlette is upgraded.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# pyasn1 0.4.8 — locked by python-jose 3.4.0
# Constraint: pyasn1<0.5.0,>=0.4.1 (hardcoded in python-jose setup.cfg)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Fyona uses JWT_ALGORITHM = "HS256" (HMAC-SHA256, symmetric key).
# pyasn1 is ONLY invoked by python-jose for asymmetric algorithms
# (RS256/ES256) that parse ASN.1-encoded keys.
# With HS256, jwt.encode() and jwt.decode() use HMAC only —
# pyasn1 is never called in any code path.
# These CVEs are all DoS via crafted ASN.1 input, but no user input
# reaches pyasn1 in Fyona's JWT flow.
#
# To remove these ignores: replace python-jose with PyJWT or authlib,
# OR upgrade python-jose to a version that allows pyasn1>=0.6.3.

CVE-2026-30922
CVE-2026-59884
CVE-2026-59885
CVE-2026-59886

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# starlette 0.41.3 — CVE-2026-48818 (SSRF via UNC paths)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# UNC paths (\\server\share) are a Windows-only feature.
# Fyona production runs on Ubuntu 24.04 (Linux).
# The SSRF vector via UNC paths is not exploitable on Linux.
#
# To remove this ignore: upgrade fastapi to >=0.133.1
# which allows starlette>=1.1.0 (fixes this CVE).

CVE-2026-48818
